      "summaries": {
        "en": "shadPS4 is an open-source PlayStation 4 emulator that enables running PS4 games on Windows, Linux, and macOS computers, making console-exclusive titles accessible on PC platforms. It's built with modern C++20 and leverages Vulkan graphics API for efficient cross-platform rendering, demonstrating how emulators can bridge hardware ecosystems through software abstraction. Developers can study its architecture to understand console emulation techniques, while users can experiment with running homebrew applications or exploring game modifications in a controlled environment.",
        "zh": "shadPS4 是一款开源 PlayStation 4 模拟器，允许在 Windows、Linux 和 macOS 系统上运行 PS4 游戏，打破了主机与 PC 之间的平台壁垒。该项目采用现代 C++20 编写，并利用 Vulkan 图形 API 实现高效的跨平台渲染，展示了如何通过软件抽象层模拟专用硬件环境。其模块化设计为开发者提供了研究游戏机系统架构和低层优化的学习范例，而用户则可在其中安全地测试自制程序或探索游戏修改可能性，是理解现代游戏系统仿真的实用工具。",
        "es": "shadPS4 is an open-source PlayStation 4 emulator that enables running PS4 games on Windows, Linux, and macOS computers, making console-exclusive titles accessible on PC platforms. It's built with modern C++20 and leverages Vulkan graphics API for efficient cross-platform rendering, demonstrating how emulators can bridge hardware ecosystems through software abstraction. Developers can study its architecture to understand console emulation techniques, while users can experiment with running homebrew applications or exploring game modifications in a controlled environment.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "shadPS4 stands out for cpp, cpp20, and emulation in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "shadPS4 is an open-source PlayStation 4 emulator that enables running PS4 games on Windows, Linux, and macOS computers, making console-exclusive titles accessible on PC platforms. It's built with modern C++20 and leverages Vulkan graphics API for efficient cross-platform rendering, demonstrating how emulators can bridge hardware ecosystems through software abstraction. Developers can study its architecture to understand console emulation techniques, while users can experiment with running homebrew applications or exploring game modifications in a controlled environment.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4 for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
