      "summaries": {
        "en": "Open-SWE is an open-source asynchronous coding agent that helps developers automate complex software engineering tasks by breaking them into manageable subtasks. It operates through a modular architecture where specialized agents handle different coding phases, enabling parallel execution and iterative refinement. Developers can integrate it into their workflows via its Python API to automate code generation, debugging, or documentation tasks, making it ideal for prototyping or accelerating development cycles.",
        "zh": "Open-SWE 是一个开源异步编码代理，旨在通过分解复杂软件工程任务来帮助开发者实现自动化。其核心采用模块化架构，不同专业代理并行处理编码各阶段，支持迭代优化，这种设计显著提升了任务执行效率。开发者可通过 Python API 将其集成到工作流中，自动完成代码生成、调试或文档编写等任务，非常适合快速原型开发或加速项目迭代，为实际工程应用提供了灵活可靠的自动化解决方案。",
        "es": "Open-SWE is an open-source asynchronous coding agent that helps developers automate complex software engineering tasks by breaking them into manageable subtasks. It operates through a modular architecture where specialized agents handle different coding phases, enabling parallel execution and iterative refinement. Developers can integrate it into their workflows via its Python API to automate code generation, debugging, or documentation tasks, making it ideal for prototyping or accelerating development cycles.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "open-swe stands out for agent, agents, and ai in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Open-SWE is an open-source asynchronous coding agent that helps developers automate complex software engineering tasks by breaking them into manageable subtasks. It operates through a modular architecture where specialized agents handle different coding phases, enabling parallel execution and iterative refinement. Developers can integrate it into their workflows via its Python API to automate code generation, debugging, or documentation tasks, making it ideal for prototyping or accelerating development cycles.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/langchain-ai/open-swe for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
